<p>
<table style="background-color:black; width:75%; border-spacing:1px" >
  <tr>
    <td colspan="3" style="color:white; font-size:10pt; width:70%; background-color:#224477; text-align:center">
      <b>Primary data sources</b>
    </td>
    <td rowspan="4">
    </td>
    <td style="white-space:nowrap; color:white; font-size:10pt; background-color:#446655; text-align:center">
      <table style="border:thin hidden;text-align:center;width:100%">
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align:center; white-space:nowrap">Query NIST Bibliographic Databases for</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="text-align:center"><b>C   V</b> (new window)</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Energy Levels:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22382&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Drake&nbsp;1985</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=11959&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Savukov&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2003</a>, <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19748&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Goryaev&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2017</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;For levels below the ionization limit, the data pertain to the isotope <sup>12</sup>C. The 1s<i>n</i>s and 1s<i>n</i>p levels with <i>n</i>&nbsp;&le;&nbsp;7 and the ionization limit are theoretical values compiled by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. Excitation energies of the 1s3d levels have been derived by A. Kramida (unpublished, 2023) from the theoretical ionization energies calculated by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22382&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Drake&nbsp;1985 </a> in three steps. First, Drake's values have been scaled to the current values of the fundamental constants (see <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22677&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Tiesinga&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2021 </a>) and atomic masses (see <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=22713&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Wang&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2021 </a>). Then these adjusted values of ionization energies were subtracted from the ground-state ionization energy calculated by <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. Finally, excitation energies of the 1s3d configuration were determined as a straight mean of four values obtained by adding Drake's adjusted 1s3p <sup>1,3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0,1,2</sub> &ndash; 1s3d <i><sup>S</sup>D<sub>J</sub></i> energy intervals to the reference values of the corresponding <sup>1,3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0,1,2</sub> levels from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. The root-mean-square deviation of the four values from the mean, combined in quadrature with the average uncertainty of the reference <sup>1,3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0,1,2</sub> levels, provided a rough estimate of the uncertainies of thus derived 1s3d <i><sup>S</sup>D<sub>J</sub></i> levels. These adjusted values were found to be in good agreement with the values derived in a similar procedure from the many-body perturbation theory (MBPT) calculations of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016 </a> for nuclear charges <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;10&ndash;36 (see below). Excitation energies of the 1s4d and 1s5d levels have been derived by A. Kramida (unpublished, 2023) from the relativistic configuration-interaction calculations of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=11959&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Savukov&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2003 </a> in two steps. First, separations of the 1s<i>nl</i> <sup>1,3</sup><i>L<sub>J</sub></i> levels (<i>n</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;3&ndash;6, <i>l</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;d, f, g) reported by Savukov&nbsp;et&nbsp;al. for nuclear charges <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;6, 7, 8, 10, 14, and 18 from the reference values of the corresponding 1s<i>n</i>p <sup>1,3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0,1,2</sub> levels (taken from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>) were isoelectronically smoothed and interpolated for all <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;6&ndash;18. Then four adjusted values were determined for each level by adding those isoelectronically smoothed separations to the corresponding reference level values of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. The root-mean-square deviation from the mean of these four values, combined in quadrature with the average uncertainty of the reference <sup>1,3</sup>P&deg;<sub>0,1,2</sub> levels, provided a rough estimate of the uncertainies of thus derived adjusted levels. For the 1s6d, 1s<i>n</i>f, and 1s<i>n</i>g (<i>n</i>&nbsp;&le;&nbsp;6) levels, the energies were derived by A. Kramida (unpublished, 2023) from the MBPT calculations of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016 </a>. Although the latter work covered only ions with nuclear charge <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;10&ndash;36, it was possible to derive the energy levels for <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;6&ndash;9 by an isoelectronic interpolation. For <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;2&ndash;5, experimental and theoretical data of sufficiently high precision exist in the literature (see references given in ASD level lists for He&nbsp;II, Li&nbsp;III, Be&nbsp;IV, and B&nbsp;V). First, the intervals between the 1s<i>nl</i> <sup>1,3</sup><i>L<sub>J</sub></i> levels (<i>n</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;3&ndash;6, <i>l</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;d, f, g) and the corresponding 1s<i>n</i>p <sup>3</sup>P<sub>0</sub> levels were calculated either from reference data for <i>Z</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;2&ndash;5 or from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19700&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Si&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2016 </a> for <i>Z</i>&nbsp;&ge;&nbsp;10. Then these intervals were interpolated along the isoelectronic sequence. The final excitation energies of the 1s<i>nl</i> <sup>1,3</sup><i>L<sub>J</sub></i> levels (<i>n</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;3&ndash;6, <i>l</i>&nbsp;=&nbsp;d, f, g) reported here were determined by adding those interpolated intervals to the reference values of the 1s<i>n</i>p <sup>3</sup>P<sub>0</sub> levels taken from <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=21139&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Yerokhin&nbsp;&&nbsp;Surzhykov&nbsp;2019 </a>. Their uncertainies were estimated by adding in quadrature the uncertainties of the reference <sup>3</sup>P<sub>0</sub> levels to the interpolation uncertainties. Several highly excited Rydberg levels have been determined by A. Kramida (unpublished, 2023) by extrapolations using the Ritz quantum defect expansion formula or the polarization formula (see their description in <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=18395&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Kramida&nbsp;2013 </a>). Uncertainties are given here for the separations from the ionization limit. The autoionizing levels are from the calculations of <a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=19748&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=E');return false">Goryaev&nbsp;et&nbsp;al.&nbsp;2017 </a>. The present data set was prepared by A. Kramida for the release of ASD v.5.11 in October, 2023.
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Elevbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=C%20V&amp;method=EL&amp;method=TE&amp;method=ND&amp;method=IP&amp;method=SF&amp;method=QF&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='C   V: bibliography energy levels query';return true;"
        onmouseout="self.status=''; return true;" target="_blank">C   V Energy Levels</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Lines:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=el&amp;db_id=6005&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=L');return false">Reader et al. 1980</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Elevbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=C%20V&amp;method=W&amp;method=CL&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='C   V: bibliography wavelengths query';return true;"
        onmouseout="self.status=''; return true;" target="_blank">C   V Line Wavelengths and Classification</a>
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class='brt1'>
      Transition Probabilities:
    </td>
    <td class='bcn'>
      &nbsp;<a onmouseover="self.status='Bibliographic Reference for C V';return true;" onmouseout="self.status='';return true;" target="_blank" href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popded('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/get_ASBib_ref.cgi?db=tp&amp;db_id=6492&amp;comment_code=&amp;element=C&amp;spectr_charge=5&amp;type=T');return false">Wiese et al. 1996</a>&nbsp;
    </td>
    <td class='blf'>
      
    </td>
    <td class='bcn1'>
      <a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="popbib('https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/ASBib1/Fvalbib/make_query.cgi?spectra=C%20V&amp;order=1');return false"
        onmouseover="self.status='C   V: bibliography transition probability query';return true;"
